  "question": {
    "text": "A ray of light along $x+\\sqrt{3}y=\\sqrt{3}$ gets reflected upon reaching $x$-axis, the equation of the reflected ray is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$y=x+\\sqrt{3}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\sqrt{3} \\mathrm{y}=\\mathrm{x}-\\sqrt{3}$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$y=\\sqrt{3} x-\\sqrt{3}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\sqrt{3} y=x-1$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\mathrm{A} \\equiv(\\sqrt{3}, 0)$\r\nLet, B $(0,1)$\r\n$\\therefore \\mathrm{B}^{\\prime} \\equiv(0,-1)$\r\n$\\therefore$ Equation of $\\mathrm{AB}^{\\prime}: \\frac{\\mathrm{y}-0}{0+1}=\\frac{\\mathrm{x}-\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{3}-0} \\Rightarrow \\sqrt{3} \\mathrm{y}=\\mathrm{x}-\\sqrt{3}$\r\n<img src=\"assets\\st0018_bbbac260281c.png\">"
  }
}